@startuml sequence
title Auth0 login to Azure Blob Storage with Workload Identity Federation

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9B458

actor User
participant "SPA\n(browser)" as SPA
participant "Auth0\n(custom domain)" as Auth0
participant "Worker\n(same origin)" as Proxy
participant "Microsoft Entra ID\nlogin.microsoftonline.com" as Entra
participant "Blob Storage" as Blob

== 1. Log in with Auth0 ==
User -> SPA : Open the app
User -> SPA : Click "Log in with Auth0"
SPA -> Auth0 : GET /authorize\n(client_id = SPA, audience = API, PKCE challenge)
Auth0 -> User : Login page
User -> Auth0 : Credentials
Auth0 --> SPA : Redirect back with ?code=...
SPA -> Auth0 : POST /oauth/token (code + PKCE verifier)
Auth0 --> SPA : Access token (JWT)
note right of Auth0
  iss = https://<custom domain>/
  aud = [API audience, /userinfo]
  azp = SPA client ID
  sub = auth0|<user id>
end note

== 2. Exchange the token for an Entra access token ==
SPA -> Proxy : POST /entra/<tenant>/token\ngrant_type = client_credentials, client_id = app registration, scope = https://storage.azure.com/.default\nclient_assertion = the Auth0 access token\n**no client secret or certificate in the browser**
note right of Proxy
  Entra refuses this request with a browser Origin header (AADSTS9002326),
  so the Worker repeats it server-side. Pass-through only: no secrets, no state.
end note
Proxy -> Entra : POST /<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/token (same form, no Origin)
Entra -> Auth0 : Fetch OIDC discovery + JWKS\n(from the federated credential's issuer)
Auth0 --> Entra : Signing keys
note over Entra
  Federated credential on the app registration checks:
  1. signature, and iss equals the credential's issuer
  2. aud equals the credential's single audience (api://AzureADTokenExchange)
     (rejects ID tokens and tokens for other APIs)
  3. sub equals the credential's subject exactly (one credential per user, no wildcards)
  azp is not checked.
end note
Entra --> Proxy : Access token for Azure Storage, issued to the app's service principal (about 1 hour)
Proxy --> SPA : Same response

== 3. Use Blob Storage with the Entra token ==
SPA -> Blob : GET /<container>?restype=container&comp=list&prefix=users/<sub>/\nAuthorization: Bearer <Entra token>, x-ms-version
Blob --> SPA : Your blobs
User -> SPA : Choose a file and upload
SPA -> Blob : PUT /<container>/users/<sub>/<file>\nx-ms-blob-type: BlockBlob
Blob --> SPA : 201 Created
note over Blob
  The app's service principal holds "Storage Blob Data Contributor" on the container.
  Every user with a federated credential acts as that one principal, so, as on GCP,
  there is no per-user prefix isolation.
end note

== 4. Token expires ==
SPA -> Auth0 : getTokenSilently() when the Entra token is within 5 minutes of expiry
Auth0 --> SPA : New access token
SPA -> Proxy : Token exchange (as in step 2)

@enduml
